From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somesh Velupally <somegupt@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:36:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] feat(qti-accesscontrol): add runtime config-image
 reader for xpu4

XPU4 targets carry no compile-time access-control tables. A signed config image is placed in DDR by an earlier boot stage and BL31 is given its base address.

Add ac_cfg.c/ac_cfg.h to validate and expose all tables from the image. Every pointer and length is bounds-checked before use to guard against a hostile or malformed image.

Add vmidmt/vmidmt_cfg_ac.c as the VMIDMT configuration provider for XPU4, satisfying vmidmt_cfg.h using tables from the image in place of cfg/${CHIPSET}/vmidmt_static_config.c used by XPU3.

Declare acc_cfg_init() in xpu_common.h so access_control.c can call it revision-agnostically. XPU3 gains a no-op stub in xpu3.c since its tables are compiled in and need no runtime setup.
  access_control.c is updated to call acc_cfg_init() before VMIDMT or XPU configuration begins.

Signed-off-by: Somesh Velupally <somegupt@qti.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/trusted-firmware-a/commit/7adfa655ffcf77fe734aa39ab661e276fbaa69c7]
Signed-off-by: Roshan Sivakumar <roshs@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
